<description>
Recover the original quadrant from a four-way mirrored rectangular panel.

Input structure
- The input is a larger background grid containing one foreground panel.
- The panel has even height and width.
- Its four quadrants are reflections of the same source pattern.

Rule
- Crop to the foreground panel's bounding box.
- Read the upper-left quadrant as the source pattern.
- Verify that the other quadrants are its left-right, up-down, and 180-degree reflections.

Key insight
- The apparent 12x12 drawing is not a pixel-scale zoom; it is a reflected 2x2 mosaic whose upper-left quadrant is the requested 4x4 image.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "foreground panel formed as a 2x2 mosaic of reflected quadrants",
  "transform": "crop to the foreground bbox and output the upper-left quadrant after verifying the other quadrants are its horizontal, vertical, and 180-degree reflections",
  "grid_shape": "half the cropped panel height by half the cropped panel width"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12x12, background 0
  panel:
    size: 8x8 (always)
    placement: anywhere on grid that fits (top-left row 0-4, col 0-4)
    rest_of_grid: all background (0)
    symmetry: full D4 (LR, UD, rot90, rot180, transpose all hold)
    structure: 2x2 mosaic of reflected copies of a 4x4 source quadrant
  quadrant:
    size: 4x4 (the upper-left quadrant of the panel = the output)
    symmetry: transpose-symmetric (q[r,c] == q[c,r])
    independent_cells: 10 (upper triangle including diagonal)
    distinct_colors: 4-7 including 0
    background_cells: 4-7 cells are 0 [observed]
    colors: non-zero colors are distinct from each other, chosen from 1-9
  output: the 4x4 upper-left quadrant of the panel

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Generate a 4x4 transpose-symmetric quadrant Q with 3-6 non-zero
       distinct colors; fill the 10 upper-triangle cells, mirror to lower
    2. Build 8x8 panel by reflecting Q into four quadrants
       (UL=Q, UR=Q flipped LR, LL=Q flipped UD, LR=Q flipped both)
    3. Create 12x12 grid of zeros; pick random top-left corner (r,c)
       with r in 0..4, c in 0..4; place 8x8 panel there
    4. Output = Q
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

